WEBVTT

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:01.840
It's gone.

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.260
It's gone.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.450
Did I drop it?

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.670
Did I lose it back then?

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.610
What are you doing?

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:10.340
Huh?

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.750
I lost something important.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.100
Want me to help you look?

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.810
It's fine. Thank you... Onii-chan.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:23.040
Don't force yourself to call me that.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.040
Just "Tenn" is fine.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.420
Tenn-san, then.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.400
Why did you agree to be adopted by Kujo-san?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.350
What about you?

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.160
He took me in in exchange for paying 
off my adoptive father's debt.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.720
I'm very grateful.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.180
My situation was similar.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.520
My parents' club was in debt,

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.570
and my younger brother was sick.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.790
Your younger brother? I see.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:52.310
From now on, I can be your prince.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.430
This is my first time 
having a younger sister.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.530
You're my second older brother.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.530
We're a strange family, aren't we?

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.040
That's for me. I'd better go.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.950
What work do you have today?

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.210
Lessons with my former younger brother.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.460
Discover...

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.470
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.680
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:25.700
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.040
Wow...

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:41.660
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:46.750
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.500
No matter what tomorrow's 
like, it won't betray us

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:57.220
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.870
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.410
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:07.850
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.400
Discover...

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.420
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:18.820
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.180
Night sky

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:24.320
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.520
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:32.130
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.420
Wow...

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.020
#09 Something Important

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.400
Thank you for coming all the way here.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.230
It's fine. Though I'll be sticking 
around to prevent any problems.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.320
Once again,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.990
R&B Group

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:00.990
I'm Tsunashi Ryunosuke.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:02.240
Thanks for having us.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:03.970
I'm Osaka Sogo.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.320
Thanks for coming!

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.200
Hey.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:06.520
Wha—

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.870
Thanks for coming, Ryu-aniki.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.870
Since you two are so good, 
I'm excited to dance with you.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.290
Let's get started!

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:13.920
Right!

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:13.920
'Kay.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.420
Pop Group

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.300
Good morning!

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:19.730
Tenn-ni—

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.730
Good morning.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:22.800
Good morning.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.680
Too gloomy. Again!

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.680
G-Good morning!

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.610
Greetings are fundamental.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.090
Pull yourselves together.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:32.810
Got it!

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.310
Rock Group

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.600
Hey!

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.290
Hey...

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:37.860
Hi.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.200
Damn it.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.990
I'm in a group with the scary Yaotome,
and Mitsu and Nagi are still off their game.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:45.530
I'll have to be the group's cushion today...

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.820
Forget about being a human.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.600
What are you mumbling about?

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.210
Oh, nothing.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:53.920
Hey, Older Izumi.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.670
You seem out of sorts recently. What's wrong?

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.170
That's not true!

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:02.740
And you've gone silent because 
he's dragging you down with him.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.550
You're more interesting when you talk.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.780
That's not true.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.760
It's Re:vale's fifth anniversary concert.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.430
Let's get pumped up!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.090
I'm impressed, Tsunashi-san.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.260
Your movements are sharp, 
and you're flexible as well.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.760
I was captivated!

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.500
Thanks.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.980
I can do that, too.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:31.500
You're right. Given your talent, 
with enough practice—

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.370
I can do it <i>right now</i>!

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:37.630
Stop!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.800
You're out of sync.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.600
Instead of worrying about your surroundings, 
you should keep time by yourself.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.550
Understood.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.930
No, you don't get it.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.900
If changing centers can 
shake you up, stay in the back.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.940
It doesn't bother me.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.030
It doesn't bother me, either.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.520
But you keep distancing yourself from me.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.210
That's not true. I...

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:04.780
Never mind. Sorry.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.680
I know I should be grateful to you.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:15.120
All right. That was pretty good.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.820
Oh, great...

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.750
Impressive, Yaotome.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:25.400
If I were like you, I bet my 
life would've been easy...

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.260
Hey, what's that supposed to mean?

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.120
I didn't mean it in a bad way.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.660
I'm just jealous, honestly.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.930
Tamaki-kun, you're being rude!

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:41.610
You know Tsunashi-san's dancing skills 
could put a professional dancer to shame!

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.150
So-chan, you keep complimenting him!

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:45.360
What?

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.190
I've been trying hard because 
you said you respected me!

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:52.200
But you keep calling <i>him</i> amazing!

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.080
When did I say I respect you?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.080
What? Forget it!

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:56.580
Huh?

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.780
How cute.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:03.460
Tamaki-kun, you're jealous because 
you want your partner's attention.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.130
Damn you, sexy beast...

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.340
<b>Sexy Beast</b>

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.340
Sexy beast?

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.010
I saw it in a magazine.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:10.390
Hey, wait...

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:15.300
And sexy dragon, and the pheromone 
prince raised on a beach resort.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:14.220
Tamaki-kun, you shouldn't say that.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.530
That's the image fabricated by the agency.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.730
Fabricated?

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:23.960
People say I'm the son of a hotel magnate,

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:27.410
but the reality is my mom just got 
remarried to a hotel proprietor.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.630
My biological father is 
a fisherman from Okinawa.

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:31.440
What?

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.620
I was going to become a fisherman, 
too, but the boat broke down.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.240
Buying my father a new boat

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:42.310
and putting my three younger brothers 
through college is my dream.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:47.160
So I relate to you and your 
search for your younger sister.

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:50.860
If there's anything I can do to help, I will.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.390
Don't be shy. Just let me know.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.840
Ryu-aniki...

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:59.060
I'm sorry. I appreciate your concern for Aya.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.140
You're such an honest kid.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.580
Tenn said something similar to me.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.300
He said success must've come easily to me

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.640
because I was born with this face and body.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.770
I hear it from others all the time, too.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:14.320
But every time, I think the same thing.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.680
You're awesome, too!

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:18.450
What could you possibly 
be dissatisfied with?

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:22.130
When you say it, it sounds sarcastic.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.790
What's sarcastic?

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.790
Do I really seem like a 
perfect success story to you?

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:27.920
Then why...

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.280
Don't I have a cute girlfriend?!

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.180
What?

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.970
You mean you don't have a bunch 
of beautiful girlfriends?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.020
See? That! Even the people
 I fall for say the same thing!

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.890
It's seriously depressing...

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.230
The same thing happened at 
last year's <i>Black or White</i>.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.650
We were desperate to win, too.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.260
We worked our butts off. 
We wanted to be supported.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:56.580
But the world cheered for IDOLiSH7.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.080
Yaotome...

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:02.060
I've never lived as anyone but me.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.450
But I do my best to live as myself.

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:07.630
I take being Yaotome Gaku 
as seriously as I can!

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.480
How about you?

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.790
Are you serious about being Izumi Mitsuki?

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:15.330
Huh? Uh, sure I am. At least, I think I am.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:19.890
But I don't know what's right 
anymore. My thoughts are a mess.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.980
You're confused because you're 
not listening to your own voice.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:25.320
My own voice?

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.900
That's right. Don't look for a right answer.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.900
Block out the noise. 
Search for your voice only.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.630
Don't try to become someone 
one hundred people love.

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:35.800
Be the version of yourself that <i>you</i> love.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:40.310
And then someday, ten thousand 
people will learn to love you.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:43.520
That's what it means to 
earnestly live as yourself.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.410
The two of you need to talk it out.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.620
Voice both your pure and
 your messy feelings.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.560
Don't be scared. You have to face them.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:57.220
The stronger the light, 
the deeper the shadows.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.900
Will you continue to avert your eyes,

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:02.180
or will you face each other and overcome?

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.080
Which exit will you choose?

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:10.200
I had no idea what I should do.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.980
I felt like I had to be grateful to you, Iori.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:20.300
But, everyone said they 
preferred Iori as the center.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:26.940
I felt like I was being rejected.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.540
Are you stupid?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.290
S-Stupid?!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:34.550
Your singing voice beats 
that of TRIGGER's Kujo Tenn!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.010
I haven't been beaten.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:40.880
Do you know what it feels like to take 
that person's place as the center?!

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:44.640
I was so scared, I could hardly bear it.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:49.150
But I became the center to help you.

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.640
So how could you think that?

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.440
What an awful thing to say...

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:54.610
Iori...

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.240
It's cruel, Nanase-san.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.380
I'm sorry. It's my fault.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.080
Forgive me, Iori.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.410
D-Don't cry.

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.160
I'm not crying!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:10.070
I didn't realize you felt the same way.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:13.120
I resented you. I was jealous.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:18.130
You fell into a pit because you 
compared yourself to others.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.220
I could never beat Yaotome Gaku.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.370
I can't beat Tsunashi Ryunosuke.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:27.200
But there's something I have 
that they'll never beat.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:32.130
You should only compare yourself 
to your own past and future selves.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.360
Show me that the people 
you are today can beat

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.320
the versions of yourselves 
who once beat us.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:40.820
Tomorrow and the day after,
keep putting in the effort to win.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.690
Let's have lunch, everyone.

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:46.080
Do you guys always eat this well?

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.130
I suppose...

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:49.490
I guess you could say...

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:52.430
I wish TRIGGER would come every day.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.320
You're not eating?

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.590
No, I will. I'll have some.

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:04.600
It's a strange feeling seeing my 
older brother in a different group.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.280
It makes you feel lonely, doesn't it?

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:07.820
I understanding how you feel.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:09.760
I always feel that way.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:11.480
We're in the same group now.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:15.560
Yeah!

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:22.500
Everyone, this afternoon we'll have an 
opportunity to see the stage at Zero Arena.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.340
Wow...

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.540
My sweet.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:33.790
Let me throw you a kiss 
filled with gratitude.

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:36.360
Nagi-san?

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.660
Wh-What's wrong?!

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.470
It's nothing...

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.710
Looking good, Tamaki-kun!

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.410
Sogo-kun, you look sexy, too!

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.350
What? Uh, thanks!

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.470
Laugh from your stomachs!

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.710
Is that the best you can do?!

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.140
No way!

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.900
Don't skip anything!
Be conscious of every movement!

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.150
Got it!

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.490
Rivals and male friendship are nice.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:01.570
Indeed.

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:06.500
There are times when it's awkward, 
stubborn, or complicated,

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:09.580
but their straightforwardness shines 
in the middle of their hearts.

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:13.990
I'm glad we were able to 
practice with TRIGGER today.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:16.460
That's how I felt after seeing their smiles.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.420
Thank you so much.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.760
No, thank you.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.500
Excuse me a moment.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.470
Hello, this is Takanashi.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:29.470
What? Really?!

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.980
What did you want to tell us?

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:36.400
The two of you have been
cast as costars in a drama.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.200
What?

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.150
Seriously?

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:40.560
Manager, are you happy?

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:41.170
Yes!

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:42.910
Then I'll do my best!

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.400
Thank you.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:47.740
The director likes the two of you.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.800
He's eager to meet you.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:53.130
See? There are people watching you.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:54.050
Yeah.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:57.540
A drama, huh? I'm not very 
confident in my acting.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:58.540
You'll be fine.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:01.090
We've invited an excellent instructor

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.800
currently working at the 
forefront of entertainment!

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.130
I'm hardly an instructor.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:09.790
It's not like I've ever 
properly studied acting.

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.630
Regardless, we'd appreciate your help!

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.100
What's it about?

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:15.710
It's a love story.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.860
The female lead is a single woman 
working in an editorial department.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.150
And them?

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:24.170
Sogo-san is the female lead's 
childhood friend and beautician.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:27.390
Tamaki-san is the boxer she 
finds at night on the street.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:30.580
Is a boxer something you can just 
find on the street at night?

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:33.620
Do you guys have any acting experience?

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:37.090
I played the pheasant in my grade 
school's production of <i>Momotaro</i>.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.080
Show me.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.250
Give me a dumpling, and I'll serve you!

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:44.990
And you, So?

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:48.570
I only acted in a play in high school.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:50.660
What kind of play was it?

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:54.060
I attended an all-boys school.
Please don't ask for more details...

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.230
Juliet, huh?

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:56.980
It was Takao Dayu.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.820
My lord, care for a smoke?

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:10.660
Not bad. Anyway, just go with that feeling.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:11.580
Later, guys.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.970
Wait, Yamato-san!

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:16.300
Won't you please instruct them?

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:18.160
There's nothing for me to teach them.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.930
It can be anything!

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:22.500
Can't you offer them some kind of advice?

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:29.040
Either imagine the feeling 
and express it outwardly

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:31.760
or memorize the expression 
to draw out the feeling.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:33.640
Use either method.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.010
What's he talking about?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.480
Why don't you actually try it?

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.900
Imagine it's your role and 
try imitating each other.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:43.230
You want me to imitate Tamaki-kun?

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.490
Sure. I can do that.

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:48.240
Tamaki-kun, it's important to 
always be five minutes early.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:47.300
<b>I'm Osaka Sogo.</b>

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:50.780
I love being five minutes early.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.540
You try it, So.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:58.780
Me, too? Um...

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.600
No, no, no, <i>no</i>!

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:00.940
<b>I'm Yotsuba Tamaki.</b>

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:00.940
What?

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.170
Like that?

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.850
I'm not like that!

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:05.840
What am I, a spoiled child?!

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:08.270
Well, what's "I love being 
five minutes early"?!

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:10.380
That's common sense,
not my personal preference!

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:13.660
Okay, okay. You both did great.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:14.140
Later.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:16.760
Wait, Yamato-san!

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:17.890
What now?

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.620
It's about the movie.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.600
Are you certain you won't accept the role?

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.810
Oh, that. I'll do it.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.570
Can't you please recon... What?

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:28.670
I said I'd do it.

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:31.820
Thank you.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:35.490
This is the birth of Takanashi 
Productions' first movie star!

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.540
Does that mean I get a reward?

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:39.500
What?

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:43.000
I think I'd like something sexy.

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:44.980
Um...

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:48.840
Like a pen that gets undressed 
when you flip it upside down?

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:49.860
<i>That's</i> what springs to mind?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.830
Mitsuki-kun, do you have a minute?

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:54.970
Huh? Sure.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:58.320
I heard you've been worried 
about MCing these days.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:15:59.840
Nagi-kun told me.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:00.980
Nagi did?

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:06.070
He asked me to help you since he can't.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:09.710
Receiving complaints is part of the job.

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:12.050
Talk too much, and people 
tell you to shut up.

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:15.520
Talk too little, and people 
say you're not doing your job.

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:17.180
It's tough, isn't it?

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:21.660
It's like being the organizer of a mixer.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.780
No matter how hard you try, nobody likes you.

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:25.610
The guy resting his chin in his hands

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:29.370
seems cooler than the guy 
busily running the event.

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:33.330
But without the organizer, there's no party.

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:36.430
Your value isn't recognized 
while you're present.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:39.410
It's noticed for the first 
time once you're gone.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:42.080
It's okay if nobody notices.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:48.100
IDOLiSH7 is a party that everyone loves
 dearly, and they can't start without you.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:51.400
Nagi! Nagi!

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.450
Oh! Mitsuki.

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:58.780
Sorry, Nagi. Mr. Shimooka-san told me.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:01.760
Did his advice cheer you up?

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:02.640
Yeah.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:03.620
Good!

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:07.710
I told you, I'm your fan.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.130
I've always supported you.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:13.750
I wanted to comfort you when you were sad.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:18.000
But you didn't want to be consoled.

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:21.300
It's because you wanted to fight.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:24.000
Nagi, thank you.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:28.890
You were worried about me, 
but I couldn't get over it.

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:30.110
I'm sorry.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:36.100
Don't worry. When I felt blue, 
I had lots of people on my side.

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:37.060
Lots of people?

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:39.820
Your fans.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.830
My fans?

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:45.830
Your fans love you.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:49.870
But even though they love 
you, they can't help you.

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:51.300
It's very painful.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:56.340
But instead of running away, 
they continued to support you.

00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:00.600
We're very blessed idols.

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:11.340
Sometimes the numerous voices 
of the city are cruel and sting.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:17.610
But if you listen closely, you'll find
 that they care for you and me.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:20.240
<b>To IDOLiSH7
 </b>From Your Fans

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:20.240
<b>Congratulations on Your Concert 
IDOLiSH7</b>

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:21.430
Believing that we'll face a brilliant future,

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:24.340
they'll raise their voices 
and continue cheering for us,

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.250
<b>Mitsuki Love</b>

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.250
<b>Nagi</b>

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:27.330
even if it's against the wind.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:32.590
With hearts stronger, tougher, 
and more valiant than ours.

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:37.100
I was suffering. I wanted to grow quickly.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:41.070
I was impatient. I'd forgotten 
the most important thing.

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:43.850
But I'll never forget again.

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:47.440
It's important to have the courage to change,

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:50.100
but it's also important to have 
the courage to remain who I am.

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:54.620
After all, I'm Izumi Mitsuki of IDOLiSH7!

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:55.900
Are you happy?

00:18:58.150 --> 00:18:59.150
Yes!

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:01.520
Yay! That's great!

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:04.330
Mitsuki, I'm hugging you with love!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.680
Oh!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.580
I-I can't breathe.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.470
Mitsuki-san, are you there?

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:10.330
It's the manager.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:12.070
I can't let her see me like this.

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:14.810
Oh! I'll hide your face with a hug.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:19.550
Um, what are you doing?

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:21.940
Pretending to be kangaroos.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:24.640
I'll pass on your message to Mitsuki.

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.990
In that case, I'll go ahead and tell you.

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:31.100
Mitsuki-san has received a new job offer.

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:32.400
What?

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:36.590
It's a voice acting job for season two 
of "Magical Girl Magical Cocona."

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:37.610
Oh?!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:40.150
Apparently the role is for 
Cocona-chan's boyfriend.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.450
He's the male lead.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.610
No!

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:47.690
That's not fair! I shall do this job!

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:49.860
Well, the offer is for Mitsuki-san...

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:53.780
My love for Cocona is greater!

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:54.920
Oh, my God!

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:59.110
Mitsuki! Please switch with me! Mitsuki!

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.740
Oh, gods of Cocona.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.430
If only I had Mitsuki's voice...

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.940
I'll get the director's autograph for you.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:16.020
It's true what they say.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:19.650
The grass is always
greener on the other side.

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:23.190
Iori, I'm sorry for everything until now.

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:24.990
How many times are you going to say that?

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:25.910
It's getting tedious.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:29.030
Well, I wasn't being considerate.

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:33.040
You seem to have everything under control, 
but you're younger and a crybaby.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.930
Don't call me a crybaby!

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:36.540
I only cried <i>once</i>!

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:39.400
I should thank Tenn-nii, too.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:42.000
He gave me a lot of advice the other day.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.550
You're right.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:44.840
Wait!

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:45.960
Momo-san!

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.690
What's going on, Tenn-nii and Momo-san?

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:57.270
Is it your voice again?

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:02.530
Is this a dream? What an awful dream.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:03.740
Ow, ow, ow.

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:07.210
That really hurts. This is really real...

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:08.530
What did the doctor say?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.640
That there's nothing wrong with me.

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:12.890
That it must be psychological.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:16.500
My heart is such a troublemaker.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.630
Do you have any idea what's causing it?

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:21.600
No idea. Momo is doing great.

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:24.360
I mean, Re:vale is successful,

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:27.760
I've got such an amazing partner,
and it's our fifth anniversary!

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:30.160
We're even the headliners 
at the inaugural concert.

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:34.940
If I'm not happy, then who is, really?

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.310
I'm king of the super ultra happy kingdom!

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:40.590
Then why did you tell Yuki-san not to come?

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:40.980
What?

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:42.860
Because...

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:45.510
It's okay. Don't worry.

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:49.920
Yuki's such a super gentleman that 
he'll forgive me if I apologize.

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:56.010
Could you leave me alone for a bit?

00:21:57.950 --> 00:21:59.080
No!

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:02.090
Riku, read the room.

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:04.150
Momo-san, please talk to us.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:08.130
Until recently, I spent a lot of 
time worrying about things on my own.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:10.230
But once I worked up the 
courage to talk about it,

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:13.100
my worries went away like 
they were nothing at all.

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:14.520
Nanase-san...

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:18.270
So don't worry about things on your own.

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:20.420
Don't force yourself to smile anymore.

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:29.280
But... But if I stop smiling,
I feel like my anxiety will crush me.

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:34.040
(If you get lost, there's a song here)

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:32.730
My happiness is borrowed.

00:22:32.730 --> 00:22:34.040
Borrowed?

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:40.040
(If you get lost, there's a song here)

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:39.320
I'm not the real Re:vale.

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:45.760
We came to understand a brilliant something

00:22:46.390 --> 00:22:51.970
resembling all the light in the galaxy

00:22:52.550 --> 00:23:04.360
Even on days I'm scared, the faint 
warmth I want to deliver won't disappear

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:10.570
Even if you want to close your 
eyes to reality's reflection

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:16.010
Come on, let's create an illusion

00:23:16.010 --> 00:23:18.660
The sound of the future

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:22.840
On the curtain of three thousand worlds

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:26.130
We quietly adorn

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:31.110
Each and every one of us has meaning

00:23:31.890 --> 00:23:35.200
It's the message of the Fantasia

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:39.740
You're the one who gave 
me the courage to weave

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:45.020
So I always want you by my side

00:23:55.680 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:55.680 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"Out of Time"</b>
